{:edb/db-before-t 1376 :edb/db-after-t 1377 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534689 50 #inst "2026-10-08T04:16:50.011Z" 13194139534689 true] [17592186087638 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303510 13194139534689 true] [17592186087638 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303518 13194139534689 true] [17592186087638 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303551 13194139534689 true] [17592186087638 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303558 13194139534689 true] [17592186087639 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303503 13194139534689 true] [17592186087639 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303537 13194139534689 true] [17592186087640 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303525 13194139534689 true] [17592186087640 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303528 13194139534689 true] [17592186087640 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303532 13194139534689 true] [17592186087640 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303544 13194139534689 true] [17592186087932 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534689 true] [17592186087932 1100 "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 8 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534689 true] [17592186087932 1100 "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}6 & 8 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139534689 false] [17592186087932 1145 "- The matrix $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $B$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(B)=6\\cdot 4-8\\cdot 3=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(B)=0,$ we conclude that $B$ is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=(-1)\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 5=-10.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $C$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ do not have an inverse." 13194139534689 true] [17592186303503 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303504 13194139534689 true] [17592186303503 1089 "q-127751" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303503 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534689 true] [17592186303503 1100 "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303503 1113 #uuid "8bc7e218-c432-5c7d-93cb-660cd4ed939b" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303503 1145 "- For the matrix $A$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(A)=(-1)\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 0=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(A)=0,$ we conclude that $A$ is not invertible. Since $A$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $A$ is singular.\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=(-2)\\cdot 5-(-3)\\cdot (3)=-1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $C$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ is singular." 13194139534689 true] [17592186303504 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303505 13194139534689 true] [17592186303504 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303506 13194139534689 true] [17592186303504 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303507 13194139534689 true] [17592186303504 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303508 13194139534689 true] [17592186303504 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303509 13194139534689 true] [17592186303504 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534689 true] [17592186303504 1041 "selection" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303504 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303506 13194139534689 true] [17592186303504 1110 #uuid "66c0f296-846d-563e-b7ef-ec9210792f71" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303505 1034 "$A$ and $C$ only" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303505 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534689 true] [17592186303505 1111 #uuid "db222ce2-d658-59e8-abed-720804bd2f85" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303506 1034 "$A$ only" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303506 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534689 true] [17592186303506 1111 #uuid "9ffc3da3-6ece-5f07-aa43-96a827f4751d" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303507 1034 "$A$ and $B$ only" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303507 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534689 true] [17592186303507 1111 #uuid "417850f7-e746-50ba-baca-15037850a3d8" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303508 1034 "$C$ only" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303508 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534689 true] [17592186303508 1111 #uuid "fa4a2fb7-63c1-5e6f-9be6-7787e63f53af" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303509 1034 "$B$ only" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303509 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534689 true] [17592186303509 1111 #uuid "4ebdb491-448d-58e9-9879-1b62216ed7af" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303510 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303511 13194139534689 true] [17592186303510 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303514 13194139534689 true] [17592186303510 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303516 13194139534689 true] [17592186303510 1089 "q-316753" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303510 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534689 true] [17592186303510 1100 "Calculate ${A}^{-1},$ where\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=\\,\\,$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} | $-2$ |  |" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303510 1113 #uuid "ca4de43e-fb29-5656-88a3-862277669b5e" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303510 1145 "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $A$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(A)=(-6)\\cdot 2-3\\cdot (-5)=3\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -(-5) & -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2/3 & -1 \\\\ 5/3 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{A}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2/3 & -1 \\\\ 5/3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {A}^{-1}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2/3 & -1 \\\\ 5/3 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-6 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303511 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303512 13194139534689 true] [17592186303511 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303513 13194139534689 true] [17592186303511 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534689 true] [17592186303511 1041 "field-1" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303511 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303512 13194139534689 true] [17592186303511 1110 #uuid "c103387a-b1a2-5b9d-b920-00f020bc9fa4" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303512 1034 "\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303512 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534689 true] [17592186303512 1111 #uuid "aeb2f2a6-b6e4-51c5-bd57-9a38c7fd1c53" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303513 1034 "2" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303513 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534689 true] [17592186303513 1111 #uuid "6b2d1a12-5ca3-57f2-aecb-39170cfe9238" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303514 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303515 13194139534689 true] [17592186303514 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534689 true] [17592186303514 1041 "field-2" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303514 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303515 13194139534689 true] [17592186303514 1110 #uuid "0f4bc053-cbd1-5f68-af31-eead6a628030" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303515 1034 "-1" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303515 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534689 true] [17592186303515 1111 #uuid "1f23df9e-6a87-594b-8fb1-effbc79fd4ae" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303516 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303517 13194139534689 true] [17592186303516 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534689 true] [17592186303516 1041 "field-3" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303516 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303517 13194139534689 true] [17592186303516 1110 #uuid "979fc8f9-5964-5ce8-bb9c-f1c2c6b7edfe" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303517 1034 "\\frac{5}{3}" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303517 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534689 true] [17592186303517 1111 #uuid "9dd88486-a7bc-5701-b4f0-0d0979c46bdb" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303518 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303519 13194139534689 true] [17592186303518 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303521 13194139534689 true] [17592186303518 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303523 13194139534689 true] [17592186303518 1089 "q-316768" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303518 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534689 true] [17592186303518 1100 "Calculate ${A}^{-1},$ where\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | $0$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=\\,\\,$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303518 1113 #uuid "6835b4df-301d-5b0d-b2b8-2bb025d353e1" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303518 1145 "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $A$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(A)=5\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot 0=-10\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-10}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1/5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1/2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{A}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1/5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1/2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {A}^{-1}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1/5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1/2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303519 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303520 13194139534689 true] [17592186303519 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534689 true] [17592186303519 1041 "field-1" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303519 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303520 13194139534689 true] [17592186303519 1110 #uuid "4fb11755-d938-5d97-835a-f02b7c3d9428" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303520 1034 "\\frac{1}{5}" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303520 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534689 true] [17592186303520 1111 #uuid "1358471d-c759-5287-a536-bdd080a221d4" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303521 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303522 13194139534689 true] [17592186303521 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534689 true] [17592186303521 1041 "field-2" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303521 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303522 13194139534689 true] [17592186303521 1110 #uuid "1e6a21f5-5a60-5523-a38a-6b9a134383c3" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303522 1034 "0" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303522 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534689 true] [17592186303522 1111 #uuid "a0c2388a-d6d7-5d5d-a4af-e901c5acbe23" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303523 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303524 13194139534689 true] [17592186303523 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534689 true] [17592186303523 1041 "field-3" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303523 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303524 13194139534689 true] [17592186303523 1110 #uuid "692ea9bf-704e-5dc4-b205-f3525dab8498" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303524 1034 "-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303524 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534689 true] [17592186303524 1111 #uuid "9cfd6101-e3d1-5b4e-9788-ecbf3618d170" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303525 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303526 13194139534689 true] [17592186303525 1089 "q-316783" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303525 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534689 true] [17592186303525 1100 "If $B=[\\begin{aligned}5x & -1 \\\\ 6x-8 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\nis a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303525 1113 #uuid "5443d517-7df6-5344-80b9-17b5b74831e0" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303525 1145 "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(5x)\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot (6x-8) \\\\  & =10x+6x-8 \\\\  & =16x-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16x-8 & =0 \\\\ 16x & =8 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303526 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303527 13194139534689 true] [17592186303526 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534689 true] [17592186303526 1041 "field-1" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303526 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303527 13194139534689 true] [17592186303526 1110 #uuid "ffa74d1b-4335-56bb-aab7-44ba0eb0ffe8" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303527 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303527 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534689 true] [17592186303527 1111 #uuid "9cb3c9e2-3c64-577f-aeb1-5d5e914b8b41" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303528 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303529 13194139534689 true] [17592186303528 1089 "q-316784" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303528 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534689 true] [17592186303528 1100 "If $B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -x+1 \\\\ 5 & 2x+7\\end{aligned}]$\nis a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303528 1113 #uuid "66c05155-e66f-5d77-9b4e-130629dd787b" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303528 1145 "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(-3)\\cdot (2x+7)-5\\cdot (-x+1) \\\\  & =-6x-21+5x-5 \\\\  & =-x-26.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x-26 & =0 \\\\ -x & =26 \\\\ x & =-26\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303529 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303530 13194139534689 true] [17592186303529 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303531 13194139534689 true] [17592186303529 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534689 true] [17592186303529 1041 "field-1" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303529 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303531 13194139534689 true] [17592186303529 1110 #uuid "f63b0cec-8348-5835-a6df-4b735dd0bcc4" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303530 1034 "26" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303530 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534689 true] [17592186303530 1111 #uuid "e3707f8a-5ad7-5365-8eae-901a4d71871c" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303531 1034 "-26" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303531 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534689 true] [17592186303531 1111 #uuid "20dea9c5-a46a-5cf9-a2e4-7aa6a62e9727" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303532 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303533 13194139534689 true] [17592186303532 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303535 13194139534689 true] [17592186303532 1089 "q-316828" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303532 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534689 true] [17592186303532 1100 "Let $B=[\\begin{aligned}2x+1 & x-40 \\\\ 1 & -x\\end{aligned}]$\nbe a singular matrix. **In ascending order**, the values of $x$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139534689 true] [17592186303532 1113 #uuid "8b310642-ede6-5a4f-a56c-989f0c39c332" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303532 1145 "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(2x+1)\\cdot (-x)-(x-40)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2{x}^{2}-x-x+40 \\\\  & =-2{x}^{2}-2x+40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}^{2}-2x+40 & =0 \\\\ -2({x}^{2}+x-20) & =0 \\\\ -2(x-4)(x+5) & =0 \\\\ x & =4,-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the values of $x$ are\n\n$$\nx=-5\\,\\text{and}\\,x=4.\n$$" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303533 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303534 13194139534689 true] [17592186303533 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534689 true] [17592186303533 1041 "field-1" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303533 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303534 13194139534689 true] [17592186303533 1110 #uuid "e3c73af9-51b6-5091-b134-07564ff2febe" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303534 1034 "-5" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303534 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534689 true] [17592186303534 1111 #uuid "b75012e3-e492-5792-9719-1d397d71cf66" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303535 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303536 13194139534689 true] [17592186303535 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534689 true] [17592186303535 1041 "field-2" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303535 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303536 13194139534689 true] [17592186303535 1110 #uuid "79908c2f-632b-513d-aa7a-fed9ae5536d8" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303536 1034 "4" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303536 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534689 true] [17592186303536 1111 #uuid "1520c08b-c044-52a0-bba9-fde2eed71cec" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303537 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303538 13194139534689 true] [17592186303537 1089 "q-71937" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303537 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534689 true] [17592186303537 1100 "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -8 & 7 & -6 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -15 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 10 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303537 1113 #uuid "ff070848-777f-5635-9918-6da54f4ec8b2" 13194139534689 true] [17592186303537 1145 "- The matrix $T$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\n- For the matrix $U$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(U)=3\\cdot 4-(-1)\\cdot (-15)=-3.\n